{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return","id":1342773,"title":"Are there any Infernal Charms that you don't expect to return?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-21T12:04:57-07:00","id":1342773,"title":"Are there any Infernal Charms that you don't expect to return?","content":"With Infernal Charms becoming Ability-based, do you expect a major shift towards &quot;Infernal Charms are techniques you perform&quot; and away from &quot;Infernal Charms are spiritual organs or mutations you grow&quot;?<br /> <br /> Do you see this changing your favorite Infernal Charms, like Verdant Emptiness Endowment?<br /> <br /> Which Ebon Shadow Dragon Charms do you expect will continue to be associated with him, as opposed to more spiteful and envious Yozi like Szoreny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:13:53-07:00","id":1342791,"title":"","content":"Not only do I expect very few of the current lineup of the Ebon Dragon's Charms to remain with him, I don't even expect them to retain the exact same theme or equivalent mechanics - even allotting for how different 3e is from 2e, I would wager that they would become nigh-unrecognizable in some circumstances, unless the developers want to keep the heavy angle on deception. As for what ends up cut that doesn't end up with Szoreny, I would expect his spite Charms to go over to Malfeas and/or Kimbery, along with the &quot;taint a memory&quot; and &quot;hide evidence of abuse&quot; Charms.<br /> <br /> Cecelyne, however, might change very little, with the primary difference being that her Charms are now Ability-based and might have a slightly different structure (they're already structured in such a way that you could probably just dump them in one Ability or another without much issue). The Whispering Flame, Adorjan, and Kimbery, too, are probably safe as is, taking in a few odds and ends from prior Yozi concepts that didn't work with their GoD writeups.<br /> <br /> Malfeas is likely to be as different from his past version as Ebby is respectively from his own, but being set as a screaming chainsaw cutter who was monopolizing the music and dance themes common to all Yozis - improperly, even, since a lot of their performances are actually quite dangerous or even lethal to be around - means that you can only really go up. He's going to get way more devious, way subtler even when he doesn't strictly need to be, and his green light is also likely to change from an on the nose analog of radiation to something weirder, like how Gervesin's illumination spreads threads of brass through the flesh of day-birds. Still Cronenbergian, perhaps, but in a different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T14:20:18-07:00","id":1342805,"title":"","content":"I think an advantage of putting the Yozis more in the background is that you can keep perfectly serviceable Charms for deception and cursing and destroying people's memories and relationships, and it's just... demonic applications of Socialize or whatever. Mixed in with some other approaches, of course. Don't want to give the wrong impression of them.<br /> <br /> Many of the Ebon Dragon Charms are good enough to survive without the Second Edition Ebon Dragon, and I don't much care to find a new Yozi to house them.<br /> <br /> I don't expect that one She Who Lives in Her Name Charm with the really long title I can't remember. It made a land that would brainwash people or something, I think the scope is too big for a Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T16:26:58-07:00","id":1342828,"title":"","content":"Given the changes to sorcery I suspect that at least some of the Sorcerous charms in Infernals will become actual sorcery spells. Not sure which ones. I haven't looked at Infernals in a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T17:46:55-07:00","id":1342844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342828#post1342828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the changes to sorcery I suspect that at least some of the Sorcerous charms in Infernals will become actual sorcery spells. Not sure which ones. I haven't looked at Infernals in a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, Lunars have Charms that basically do the same thing without designating themselves with a Keyword or being vulnerable to countermagic... which is no longer a thing anyway. They just make the Duration Instant while including a time limit.<br /> <br /> Solars don't really have Charms like that, but I think the design principle is still sound for many Infernal Charms.<br /> <br /> There were Malfeas Charms to make you nigh immune to influence, those are right out, although I think some of the look and fluff could be salvaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T18:47:52-07:00","id":1342851,"title":"","content":"Swallowing the Scorpion and the whole Devil Tiger tree are probably going away (though I hope some of the names stick as a few of them were cool). We're also pretty likely not to have that one charm that dragged information out of a least god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T22:14:46-07:00","id":1342876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342805#post1342805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't expect that one She Who Lives in Her Name Charm with the really long title I can't remember. It made a land that would brainwash people or something, I think the scope is too big for a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiralty Prohibition Index?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T00:16:26-07:00","id":1342891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342851#post1342851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swallowing the Scorpion and the whole Devil Tiger tree are probably going away (though I hope some of the names stick as a few of them were cool). We're also pretty likely not to have that one charm that dragged information out of a least god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance's said they'll at least be keeping the concepts for Spirit of the Living World (creating a world in your soul) and Path of a Thousand Whispers (creating demons from aspects of your psyche).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T05:35:00-07:00","id":1342923,"title":"","content":"Must admit that i never thought much about the subject of infernal charms between editions and what might or not get the axe - i have yet to delve really deep in mechanic changes between editions, specially considering that while i liked many concepts involved with them, my practical experience with the GSPs was minimal. I kind of doubt the change in portrayal &amp; themes of some of the Yozis will have much of an impact in what will be cut or not - some fluff gymnastics might come up due to changed focus and orientations (is becoming a devil-tiger/embrionary neo-yozi still a thing?) but most charm concepts and tricks should stay where sound and fun i guess.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous charms should be no big deal and might even be seen as obsolete in some aspects with the kind of expansion and updates Ssorcery as a whole got in 3e, with Initiations, sorcerous merits, shaping rituals, control spells &amp; a few charms peppered across the books when it comes to customization/theming of an individual's personal sorcerous journey of discovery.<br /> <br /> Overall i'm in no rush to deal with them at the moment - there's more than enough to tinker with and develop in renovated/updated Creation at the moment while the writers take their time with the other exalts, old and brand new (as an aside, i have toyed with the idea of writing some &quot;Apocryphals&quot; based on the alternate takes from Burn Legend or other setting from Shards of the Exalted Dream, but that is still for very, very far away in the future).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342891#post1342891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vance's said they'll at least be keeping the concepts for Spirit of the Living World (creating a world in your soul) and Path of a Thousand Whispers (creating demons from aspects of your psyche).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe my mind is just taking a funny bender, but i have been seeing hints of such posssibilities in the Solar occult charm tree, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2019, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T05:49:37-07:00","id":1342926,"title":"","content":"I expect the Clarity Prohbition Index and the Desert Ceclyne charm might be condensed into something like Wyld Shaping Technique","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T06:56:38-07:00","id":1342935,"title":"","content":"While we haven't gotten that far along, I suspect that any Sorcerous Charms that make it into Ex3 will stay Infernal Charms, and just lose the vulnerability to countermagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T09:02:27-07:00","id":1342954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342891#post1342891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance's said they'll at least be keeping the concepts for Spirit of the Living World (creating a world in your soul) and Path of a Thousand Whispers (creating demons from aspects of your psyche).</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone eagerly awaiting the day that <i>Indivisible </i>becomes available on the Nintendo Switch, I would be disappointed if Ajna and her Incarnations and her Heruka form either don't inspire Infernal Exalted or are coincidentally possible with Infernal Exalt.<br /> <br /> Ajna's Heruka form is easily a Shintai, and her Incarnations might be the Infernal answer to Solar personae, whether the Incarnations are demons or something more human.<br /> <br /> See, I'm totally assuming that Ajna is the reincarnation of some divine being who incarnated into multiple other humans, with Ajna merely being the central piece.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:23:30-07:00","id":1343062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342876#post1342876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chiralty Prohibition Index?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gesundheit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342923#post1342923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorcerous charms should be no big deal and might even be seen as obsolete in some aspects with the kind of expansion and updates Ssorcery as a whole got in 3e, with Initiations, sorcerous merits, shaping rituals, control spells &amp; a few charms peppered across the books when it comes to customization/theming of an individual's personal sorcerous journey of discovery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms with the Sorcerous Keyword weren't really in competition with actual sorcery, I think. It strikes me as having been more a case of exploring new Charm technology towards a point of allowing Infernals to deal out characteristic afflictions without committing their mote pool into nothing, as well as a bit of... consideration for the subject of Primordials originating sorcery that was introduced in that Edition.<br /> <br /> As I said, Lunars also have a concern with throwing out native blessings and curses, and do basically the exact same thing without making as big a deal out of it. I can't really buy &quot;Infernals won't have Charms to do ancient evil sorcerer king shit because they could learn spells for that&quot; when Lunars are given a Charm to make a spot that will convert beastfolk rather than being told to become a sorcerer and use workings.<br /> <br /> You know, there are things that come with the Infernal package that they should get in their own right; they should not be obligated to become sorcerers in order to do things that we would expect of them.<br /> <br /> Second Edition balanced ongoing Charms without commitment by making them vulnerable to being countered and dispelled, but Third Edition has found alternative methods of limitation at the same time as it realized that one-stop dispellation was very boring and dropped it for actual spells, so I say it's fine either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1342926#post1342926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the Clarity Prohbition Index and the Desert Ceclyne charm might be condensed into something like Wyld Shaping Technique</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that I wasn't fully articulating the problem, but when part of my issue with the former Charm was that it was far too wordy, I certainly wouldn't want it to have something else added to the mix and then modelled off of the single most wordy Charm ever <i>and</i> made available to function in more frequent places than the Wyld.<br /> <br /> That being said, reminding myself of Lunar Charms that created areas with mystical properties makes me revise my position on the place of the Charm in question in terms of whether that kind of scope is appropriate. There's a precedent, and that's the last I'll say on it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:50:33-07:00","id":1343072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343062#post1343062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charms with the Sorcerous Keyword weren't really in competition with actual sorcery, I think. It strikes me as having been more a case of exploring new Charm technology towards a point of allowing Infernals to deal out characteristic afflictions without committing their mote pool into nothing, as well as a bit of... consideration for the subject of Primordials originating sorcery that was introduced in that Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, i never meant such an opposition in any way, my bad if i gave such an impression by mistake.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more along the lines of how consideration for the subject of Primordials originating sorcery was used as a springboard to explore expansions and a degree of theming in sorcery and a variety of related effects through the infernal charmset, venues that in 3e edition are now at least in part covered by the new Sorcery mechanics like initiation styles, shaping rituals and related supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> More a matter of intercession between them and possible &quot;obsolescence&quot; so to speak of Sorcerous Keyword charms as an &quot;infernal thing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-22-2019, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T02:01:51-07:00","id":1343106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343072#post1343072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, i never meant such an opposition in any way, my bad if i gave such an impression by mistake.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more along the lines of how consideration for the subject of Primordials originating sorcery was used as a springboard to explore expansions and a degree of theming in sorcery and a variety of related effects through the infernal charmset, venues that in 3e edition are now at least in part covered by the new Sorcery mechanics like initiation styles, shaping rituals and related supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> More a matter of intercession between them and possible &amp;quot;obsolescence&amp;quot; so to speak of Sorcerous Keyword charms as an &amp;quot;infernal thing&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're misremembering the Keyword as designating the six different Sorcerous Enlightenment of (Yozi) Charms. That Charm does have the Keyword (for some reason, it doesn't actually have a function there), but they're not what the Keyword is about. When talking about it, I have not been talking about how they would initiate into sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T04:12:27-07:00","id":1343121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343106#post1343106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're misremembering the Keyword as designating the six different Sorcerous Enlightenment of (Yozi) Charms. That Charm does have the Keyword (for some reason, it doesn't actually have a function there), but they're not what the Keyword is about. When talking about it, I have not been talking about how they would initiate into sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It has been a few years since i last used Infernals, so you might be correct. I have yet to reread, but the Keyword's theme might have been somewhat vague beside the common vulnerability to Countermagic that ain't quite a thing in 3e anymore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T05:26:08-07:00","id":1343133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343121#post1343121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have yet to reread, but the Keyword's theme might have been somewhat vague beside the common vulnerability to Countermagic</div> </div> </div> </div>Internals got to imbue harmful or helpful magic into people, objects or places without needing to commit motes of Essence for the Duration. Virtually everything with the Keyword did that. There are a couple of times it's attached to some kind of energy blast attacks where the point seems to be providing an additional form of defence, but the format is fairly consistent.<br /> <br /> Hence we get gameplay shaped towards freely allowing Green Sun Princes to throw around curses and creepy blessings. As I've said, increasing the witch look to Lunars entailed them also getting in on some of that, and it just came up with Instant Charms whose text included a time limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T05:58:32-07:00","id":1343142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343133#post1343133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Internals </b>got to imbue harmful or helpful magic into people, objects or places without needing to commit motes of Essence for the Duration. Virtually everything with the Keyword did that. There are a couple of times it's attached to some kind of energy blast attacks where the point seems to be providing an additional form of defence, but the format is fairly consistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Passive-Agressive Red Tape Fettering Arts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But now more seriously, that's an interesting reading of what the old keyword ensued in gameplay. can't say i ever got that from reading on it in book, but then i probably focused more on the summary than actually exploring themes of the charms themselves. That and the one time i actually made use of the Keyword it was a sort of springboard/excuse to adapt a number of abandoned 1e spells into the charmset of a homebrew primordial, so, not really looking that hard as i might otherwise, i guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343133#post1343133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence we get gameplay shaped towards freely allowing Green Sun Princes to throw around curses and creepy blessings. As I've said, increasing the witch look to Lunars entailed them also getting in on some of that, and it just came up with Instant Charms whose text included a time limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something to better look into the future, there's much in the way of new charm shenanigans and new venues being explored with each exalt that i have to catch up to yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T08:43:35-07:00","id":1343186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343142#post1343142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can't say i ever got that from reading on it in book, but then i probably focused more on the summary than actually exploring themes of the charms themselves. </div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> odd how the Keyword description opted to place the weakness before the point about how its motes are not committed, and doesn't provide a standard for the kinds of Charms that it goes on.<br /> <br /> But that being the allowance provided by those Charms did stand out to me from early on, because the matter of how much magic somebody can keep running at once often strikes me as a central consideration, so Infernals having Charms that they could throw out ultimately without limit seemed like a significant key detail. I found it to have significant implications for the scope they could operate on and degree to which they didn't need to be discerning.<br /> <br /> Charms strongly concerned with Virtues being shared for the chop should go without saying. That may also go for Charms that shape the Exalt's values in general; the Intimacy system already has significant plasticity, and designating anything like specific Ties and Principles they might get strikes me as somewhere between overtly constraining and kind of inconsequential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T17:58:35-07:00","id":1343312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343186#post1343186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Charms strongly concerned with Virtues being shared for the chop should go without saying. That may also go for Charms that shape the Exalt's values in general; the Intimacy system already has significant plasticity, and designating anything like specific Ties and Principles they might get strikes me as somewhere between overtly constraining and kind of inconsequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtues in previous editions had even more of a connection with spirit and raksha charms - though through the abstraction of Graces in the later case - and i sometimes ask myself how its absence might change (or not) the flavor and charm mechanics of either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T06:17:00-07:00","id":1343395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343312#post1343312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Virtues in previous editions had even more of a connection with spirit charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit Charms opted to categorise themselves by Virtues in the absence of any other factor. Linking those categories by Virtues was not completely arbitrary, for instance the more offensive Charms or under Valor, but they didn't really have anything to do with the Virtues as character qualities.<br /> <br /> I am referring to the Infernal Charms that altered how the actual Virtues worked, such as changing the circumstances in which you needed to roll Compassion. This to represent the capacity of Yozi Charms to alter one's humanity.<br /> <br /> Third Edition doesn't approach representing people's values in that manner, so if such transformative Charms were still around, their priorities would shift dramatically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">i sometimes ask myself how its absence might change (or not) the flavor and charm mechanics of either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits have no Charm lists, so there's no need to categorise them. All spirits get their own Charms.<br /> <br /> Not a change precipitated on the removal of Virtues, mind. Spirits were already getting that because it's better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T07:07:03-07:00","id":1343404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1343395#post1343395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirit Charms opted to categorise themselves by Virtues in the absence of any other factor. Linking those categories by Virtues was not completely arbitrary, for instance the more offensive Charms or under Valor, but they didn't really have anything to do with the Virtues as character qualities.<br /> <br /> I am referring to the Infernal Charms that altered how the actual Virtues worked, such as changing the circumstances in which you needed to roll Compassion. This to represent the capacity of Yozi Charms to alter one's humanity.<br /> <br /> Third Edition doesn't approach representing people's values in that manner, so if such transformative Charms were still around, their priorities would shift dramatically.<br /> <br /> Spirits have no Charm lists, so there's no need to categorise them. All spirits get their own Charms.<br /> <br /> Not a change precipitated on the removal of Virtues, mind. Spirits were already getting that because it's better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did remember what charms you meant but the subject of Virtues and their full replacement by the updated Intimacy system got me thinking of other things (spirit &amp; fae charms) vaguely related to Virtues - and how Intimacies might or not be used to flavor them in the future and from threre i ran into a bender of sorts might be said.<br /> <br /> But it is as you said, while not <i>completely</i> arbitrary, Virtues were never strongly tied in flavoring or theming either spirit or raksha charms more of a &quot;coat hanger&quot; holding them all in one place, so to speak.<br /> <br /> The intimacy system might offer a much greater potential in relation to flavoring of charms, but i suspect trying to bolt any charmset onto them could end up as more replacing a straightjacket with another than a springboard to launch ideas from. Having no charm lists for spirits but guidelines like for evocations or future Exigent charms might be for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:55:53-07:00","id":1344611,"title":"","content":"Murder is Meat maybe? The name is anachronistic and the inversion of the slogan Meat is Murder is potentially alienating. Extra motes potentially breaks the game and \u201cI don\u2019t consider mortals people\u201d could be achieved better elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T04:41:51-07:00","id":1344892,"title":"","content":"I agree a lot of the Ebon Dragon charms will not be Ebon Dragon, but there's a number I'd hope that would stay - primarily Golden Years Turned Black and related charms.<br /> <br /> Also, while I look forward to seeing Malfeas expanding (maybe the rough effect of some of the old Theion charms from Shards could inspire a few?) I really do hope some of the core of the combat tree stays; being able to add mutations (as per By Rage Recast... I think that was the one?) or turn into a big stone version of yourself, and so forth. And, of course, green radiation lasers. (Oooh, also, Kneel or Be Knelt or something more general.)<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is the exact inverse of what the thread is asking, but it's much easier for me to think of the bits I want to <i>keep</i> as opposed to the bits that ought to be tossed out, in this case<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T04:44:51-07:00","id":1345199,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to being liberated from the old Yozi centric structure than I feel limited a lot of creative ideas.<br /> How many people actually had a use for Witness to Darkness as oppose to accepting it wasn't <i>that</i> bad and necessary to further their progression into the charm tree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 11-01-2019, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T07:49:41-07:00","id":1345233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1345199#post1345199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to being liberated from the old Yozi centric structure than I feel limited a lot of creative ideas.<br /> How many people actually had a use for Witness to Darkness as oppose to accepting it wasn't <i>that</i> bad and necessary to further their progression into the charm tree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Malfeas' Nightmare Fugue thing. He was also really insistent that the only weapons you could form from green hellfire were spears.<br /> <br /> <br /> What about Infernal Monster Style, though? Does anyone want to see that return as a Style any Exalt can learn, or as Infernal-exclusive Brawl, Resistance, and Athletics Charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T08:39:04-07:00","id":1345241,"title":"","content":"I don't think vee will be left there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T09:26:13-07:00","id":1345247,"title":"","content":"God sake, forum eating a short but intricate post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1344892#post1344892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really do hope some of the core of the combat tree stays; being able to add mutations (as per By Rage Recast... I think that was the one?) or turn into a big stone version of yourself, and so forth. <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mutations weren't really the core of their combat tree.<br /> <br /> I expect that they'll get different means of modelling big demonic transformations now. There are better Charms to follow the lead of, and whole mutations are better than they were before, I don't think they write cover the image I would expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:05:04-08:00","id":1345797,"title":"","content":"How do you figure Mind-Hand Manipulation might return?<br /> <br /> Archery Charms is a possibility. Archery Charms have always evoked &quot;trick arrows&quot; for Solars, Terrestrials, and Sidereals. Mind-Hand Meditation had so many upgrades that allowed you to change the telekinesis into other forms of energy or physical substances, or to transform people killed with it into other materials. Seems very adaptable and versatile to me, and of course range is the name of the game.<br /> <br /> Cecelyne's sand-blasting Charms might be found in Thrown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:11:07-08:00","id":1345800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1345797#post1345797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you figure Mind-Hand Manipulation might return?<br /> <br /> Archery Charms is a possibility. Archery Charms have always evoked &quot;trick arrows&quot; for Solars, Terrestrials, and Sidereals. Mind-Hand Meditation had so many upgrades that allowed you to change the telekinesis into other forms of energy or physical substances, or to transform people killed with it into other materials. Seems very adaptable and versatile to me, and of course range is the name of the game.<br /> <br /> Cecelyne's sand-blasting Charms might be found in Thrown.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Vance has said that Mind-Hand Manipulation would make a lot of sense as a SWLiHN-inspired Athletics Charm, potentially being purchasable from Occult instead (like how Totemic or Bridge work I think). And yeah, sand blasts are proooobably Thrown","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:17:21-08:00","id":1346497,"title":"","content":"Man, I loved Witness to Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T04:12:48-08:00","id":1346692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1342773-are-there-any-infernal-charms-that-you-don-t-expect-to-return?p=1346497#post1346497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I loved Witness to Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious what you were doing with it, because to me it and Demonic Primacy of Essence were flaws that we paid xp for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}